4},{"week":6,"opponent":"NYJ","home":true,"pf":26.0,"pa":19.0,"off_snaps":67,"epa_per_play":0.01227,"pass_rate":0.4776,"pass_rate_neutral":0.54,"def_epa_per_play":-0.03686}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2023,"team":"DET","distance":0.6687,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2023,"team":"HOU","distance":0.6704,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Bobby Slowik"},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.683,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kyle Shanahan"},{"season":2022,"team":"LV","distance":0.6929,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Josh McDaniels"},{"season":2024,"team":"BAL","distance":0.6931,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"PIT","distance":0.2164,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.3282,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"MIA","distance":0.3978,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"DAL","distance":0.4598,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.4853,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Patriots are 4-2 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 136 to 113. The offense ranks 11th in EPA per play and the defense 18th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd lowest no-huddle rate in the league.","offense":"The Patriots offense has been a little above average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd lowest no-huddle rate in the league. Drake Maye has run the passing game, with DeMario Douglas leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Patriots defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 14th and 25th. Elijah Ponder has led the way with 5.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 5th highest in the league.","special":"The Patriots have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 80% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 19% of the money on the books. Their quarterbacks were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Drake Maye has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,463 yards. Targets have been spread around, with DeMario Douglas and Romeo Doubs leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Rhamondre Stevenson and TreVeyon Henderson. On defense, Elijah Ponder leads the team with 5.5 sacks.","coaching":"Josh McDaniels is calling the offense and Zak Kuhr is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Lions under Ben Johnson and the 2023 Texans under Bobby Slowik. Their defense looks most like the 2025 and 2024 Steelers.","trends":"The offense went from 1st in EPA per play in 2025 to 11th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 11th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 18th so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 4% to 8%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}